# The visual review harness and what it renders.
#
# `extension/.review/` holds a tool that lays the panel out in headless
# Chromium so UI work can be looked at rather than inferred. Whether it becomes
# a permanent visual-regression tool is a separate decision, so the tool itself
# is deliberately untracked for now — but its output is many megabytes of
# generated HTML and PNGs, and these lines are what stop a stray `git add .`
# from committing them.
extension/.review/

# A developer's own retrieval corpus: real issue text and the files that fixed
# it. Internal Jira prose does not belong in a public repository, so the format
# and the loader are committed and the cases are not. `python
# tests/retrieval_corpus.py --format` prints the shape.
tests/retrieval_corpus/

# The real forbidden-word list for tests/test_publishable.py. Local only: a
# guard that names a company in a public repository discloses the thing it
# exists to keep out. `tests/forbidden_words.example` is the committed template.
tests/forbidden_words.txt
